In the above code, if left part becomes smaller, then we make recursive call for left part. Else for the right part. In worst case (for space), when both parts are of equal sizes in all recursive calls, we use O(Log n) extra space. Reference: https://www.cs.nthu.edu.tw/~wkhon/algo08-tutorials/tutorial2b.pdfThis article is contributed by Dheeraj Jain.
